# Scale Studio — one viewport, no scroll

Core practice functionality must always fit inside **one viewport** (`100dvh` / `StudioViewport`) with **no vertical scrolling**.

## Must stay visible without scrolling

- Just play / Pick notes mode switch
- Pick notes controls (key, Major/Minor, octave, direction) when active
- Scale title and notation area
- Recording controls (Record/Import, mic, record button / timer)
- Progress bar

## Layout rules

- Prefer compressing gaps, padding, and control heights with `clamp()` / viewport units over adding scroll.
- Notation absorbs height changes (`flex: 1`, `min-height: 0`); capture stays `flex-shrink: 0` under the notes column.
- Switching Just play ↔ Pick notes must not push recording off-screen or require scrolling.
- Do not introduce page-level or shell-level vertical scroll for the ready/practice state.
- Test common laptop heights: 768px, 800px, 900px, and MacBook-sized displays.
